  "known_limitations": [
    "PTC headlines: titles of 2017-2019 news articles annotated span by span by professional annotators (Da San Martino et al., CC-BY-4.0). Every train-article title is used, no sampling; PTC was never used for prompt tuning.",
    "PTC headlines: no_technique means the annotators marked no propaganda span in the title, not a separate neutrality judgement. Titles were annotated inside the whole article and some clearly loaded titles carry no span, so part of the false positives here may be label noise.",
    "Real news headlines, human-annotated (PTC, SemEval-2020 Task 11), eval_v3: small samples for appeal_to_fear n=3, exaggeration_minimization n=3, doubt n=7, vague_authority n=1, changing_subject n=1; their per-technique numbers have very wide intervals.",
    "SemEval-2021 Task 6 texts are meme captions, not news headlines: a domain shift from the headlines the product is built for.",
    "SemEval-2021 Task 6: no_technique means the upstream annotators marked no propaganda span in the text; it was not separately judged as neutral.",
    "SemEval-2021 Task 6 (meme texts), eval_v3: 48 texts with two or more of our six techniques were excluded (a single reference label would be arbitrary); 17 texts with only out-of-taxonomy techniques were excluded.",
    "SemEval-2021 Task 6 (meme texts), eval_v3: small samples for appeal_to_fear n=2, exaggeration_minimization n=8, vague_authority n=2, changing_subject n=4; their per-technique numbers have very wide intervals.",
    "Real news headlines: the labels come from ONE LLM annotator, not from humans, and there is no second annotator, so label noise is unknown and no human ceiling (Cohen's kappa) exists. The annotator and the ensemble's models are all general-purpose LLMs, so their errors may be correlated and agreement may be overstated.",
    "Real news headlines: the annotator labelled from the headline text alone, before seeing any ensemble output, but picked the 70 headlines from a random sample of 140, so the set is not a random sample of all news and borderline cases were mostly left out. This is a stopgap until two human annotators label a gold set.",
    "Real news headlines, labelled by one LLM annotator (not human), eval_v3: small samples for appeal_to_fear n=3, exaggeration_minimization n=4, doubt n=4, vague_authority n=1, changing_subject n=1; their per-technique numbers have very wide intervals.",
    "Public datasets may be part of the models' training data (possible leakage), which can inflate scores.",
    "Techniques outside our six are not measured: texts with only such techniques are excluded, not relabelled as no_technique.",
    "Agreement (3/3, 2/3) is the share of models that voted for the final technique, not a calibrated probability.",
    "F1 and macro-F1 are not simple proportions: macro-F1 and span token-F1 intervals are a percentile bootstrap over examples, 2000 resamples, seed 0; all other intervals are Wilson 95%.",
    "Span token-F1 is averaged over every example with a technique reference and reference spans, whatever the predicted technique; the value restricted to correctly classified examples is reported as span_token_f1.when_technique_correct.",
    "Human ceiling (Cohen's kappa between two independent annotators) is not measured yet: there is no second annotation."
  ],
  "definitions": {
    "accuracy": "share of examples whose ensemble technique equals the reference",
    "fpr_no_technique": "share of no_technique references for which the ensemble predicted some technique",
    "macro_f1": "mean F1 over labels that occur as reference or prediction in the source",
    "f1": "2*tp / (support + predicted)",
    "by_agreement": "accuracy grouped by votes for the final technique; disputed verdicts carry no_technique",
    "flag_policies": "a text is flagged when the ensemble names a technique with at least min_agreement votes",
    "per_model": "each model over its valid votes; missing votes are counted in n_missing_votes",
    "n": "examples scored; failed classifications are counted in n_errors and excluded"
  }
}
